### Manual lease persistence package independent review

- Review: Read `.agents/skills/code-simplifier/SKILL.md`, manual-session requirements MB-03/04/05/07/10/11 and design §7, `storage/database.py`, `storage/manual.py`, and the scoped persistence tests. Schema v4 adds one installation-wide partial unique index over provisioning/active/closing/recovering leases. `BEGIN IMMEDIATE` serializes acquisition across connections/processes; same owner, personal session, profile, run, and host retries return the existing row, while busy errors remain generic. The lease deliberately has no cascading FK to account/session rows, so logout cannot free a potentially live helper. Transitions and closure CAS-match session, owner, personal session, profile, run, host, and expected state/helper identity. Helper liveness is probed before opening the close transaction, and only confirmed-dead results close the retained locator; `LIVE`, `UNKNOWN`, and probe errors keep the slot occupied. All DAO timestamps are finite numeric UTC epoch seconds, acquisition validates expiry/deadline ordering, and helper identity is omitted from record repr. The DAO remains a persistence boundary without VNC or service/runtime responsibilities. Code-simplifier review found no clarity or scope change warranted.
