## Uncapped fork code review — 2026-11-07

- Scope: all fork-owned production code and tests at baseline `17405c9a927330af4bf96b29e89b8e8315518341` relative to upstream `530b993ff3a7d211aaa0904fba0817b77c75d4c9`; unchanged upstream and bundled noVNC excluded from review. The requested effort is `xhigh --fix`, with no cap on confirmed corrections. Original independent module/angle review and gap sweep were recovered from the interrupted thread; closure checks use independent reviewers for runtime, transfers and desktop/API/MCP. Design order: Pragmatic DDD (DAO/DTO), SRP, KISS/YAGNI, DRY.
- Parent-owned corrections: Windows catalog locking now retries the nonblocking primitive until the caller's deadline (or indefinitely when none was supplied), without swallowing unrelated OS errors. Batch authorization builds one current catalog index under the existing lock rather than reloading once per target. Compatibility checks share a per-invocation parsed-source cache; synthetic admission drift still fails against the extracted `_prepare_and_start` launch site.
- Deployment/example and acceptance corrections: the proxy example preserves supported large imports instead of imposing an unrelated 20 MiB limit; smoke cleanup attempts every established personal logout, checks status and transport failures, and preserves an existing smoke exception. No real service was operated.
- Existing-spec contradictions were resolved to the already implemented Argon2id dependency, bubblewrap adapter and same-origin cookie/Origin/CSRF contracts. No new deployment or transport alternative was introduced. Required live cases remain unchecked; this code review does not authorize a completion claim for slice 9 or archival.
- Code Simplifier applied to the parent-owned changed blocks. Existing DAO/DTO and concrete service boundaries are preserved; the cache and catalog maps remove repeated work without a new framework or fallback compatibility path. Initial focused verification reached 86 passed and one stale diagnostic expectation; updating that expectation to the relocated launch hook passed its targeted rerun. Integrated candidate verification and independent closure receipts follow below.
